        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute a deterministic hash value in [0, 1) for the node. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Uses std::hash on the concatenation of version + node_id. NOTE: std::hash&lt;std::string&gt; is consistent within a single binary but is implementation-defined across different compilers/platforms. Since all nodes in a cluster run the same binary when evaluating canary membership, this is sufficient for single-binary deployments. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/updates/canary_rollout.h" line="280" column="12" bodyfile="src/updates/canary_rollout.cpp" bodystart="83" bodyend="91"/>
